<!--
  Intentional API break in 0.7.0: CsvValidationResult was converted from a
  `public sealed record` to a `public sealed class` with two explicit
  constructors (one for success, one for failure). The redesign eliminates
  the null-failures bypass and makes illegal states unrepresentable.

  Consequence: the compiler-synthesized record members below are gone from
  the assembly surface. Consumers that used the primary ctor `(bool,
  IReadOnlyList<string>)`, Deconstruct, ==/!=, or the record's IEquatable
  implementation get a compile-time error and must switch to `Pass`,
  `Fail(...)`, or the new `CsvValidationResult(IReadOnlyList<string>)` ctor.
  See CHANGELOG.md and the release PR for migration notes.
-->
